ves-a-later-required-item bug documented in BMB-2026.json's notes), Department List C generic placeholders, and the MATH 231 confirmation for department list B, unchanged. The MATH 3->4->21->22 prereq-chain fix and the CHEM 450 self-referencing prereq_groups (['CHEM 450'] plus ['CHE 320']) / BMB 474 concurrent_groups block flagged in BMB-2026.json's own notes are properties of this engine's shared, non-year-specific scraped course catalog (load_merged_catalog draws from current course-catalog data regardless of catalog_year, not from a per-archive-year scrape), not of this specific archived bulletin edition -- so they reproduce identically here. The same fix (explicit MATH 3/MATH 4 in Semester 1, MATH 21/MATH 22 in Semester 2) is required and applied for this year's plan to build cleanly, and the same grad_years=7 (10 simulated terms / 5 years) minimum applies, for the same reason documented at length in BMB-2026.json: BMB's own critical path (MATH 3->4->21->22 -> CHEM 110 -> CHEM 112/MICRB 201 -> BMB 251 -> BMB 252 -> BMB 400/401/442 -> BMB 402/443W -> BMB 445W/448 -> BMB 474) is a genuine 10-term-deep sequential chain, confirmed clean only at grad_years=7, not grad_years=4 -- not a credit-capacity problem.",
